  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.24 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.40 (a Wasm sub-view copy fix; a workaround for a Mono wasm interpreter bug that aborted browser pages). TRELLIS.2 image to 3D now completes on slower GPUs in the browser (an RX 590 in Chrome: before, the device was lost every run): every model block is its own WebGPU command buffer, and the distance searches and decoder convolutions run in chunks, so no submission nears the Windows 2 s GPU watchdog (bit-identical results; Trellis2ImageTo3D.Trace finds a hang); Wan 2.2's transformer likewise ends a command buffer per block in the browser. Hugging Face files resolve once per file instead of once per range request (the Hub allows 3,000 resolver calls per 5 minutes; a streamed 27 GB checkpoint spent ~1,700). The exact tensor-core attention keeps q, k, v and the probabilities as fp16 halves at power-of-two scales: fp32 accuracy at the same speed (it was 15x the fp32 kernel's error). LTX-2 keyframe-guided attention runs on the tensor cores (3x faster; TRELLIS2_MMA_BIAS_ATTN=0 turns it off). See CHANGELOG.md.",
